    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        248,
        1400,
        1916,
        1636
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The State, the City and the New York City Transit Authority are entering into agreements under the terms of which the Transit Authority is to design, equip and construct eight rapid transit routes and design five additional rapid transit routes in the City.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2487,
          "min": -1.4375
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 46,
          "mean": -0.0001,
          "min": -0.0007
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 13160,
        "area_px": 381140,
        "density": 0.03453,
        "chars": 257,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 19.53
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        248,
        1678,
        1940,
        1912
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "These projects will be financed by the City, with State aid of $600 million from the proceeds of the transportation bond issue approved by the voters in 1967. Other mass transit projects presently being considered will be financed with City funds or such other funds as become available.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2358,
          "min": -1.2931
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 58,
          "mean": -0.0025,
          "min": -0.1395
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 16381,
        "area_px": 383526,
        "density": 0.04271,
        "chars": 287,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 17.52
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        248,
        1954,
        2072,
        2373
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The design, and subsequent construction of the various subway routes will involve modification, relocation or restoration of City-owned facilities other than Transit. In order to reduce to a minimum the potential dislocation of such City facilities and resulting inconvenience to the people of New York City, it is important to coordinate the requirements of the various City agencies whose facilities may be affected by the Transit Authority project designs and construction. Mayor Lindsay accordingly has issued the following directive:",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2366,
          "min": -1.7197
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 87,
          "mean": -0.001,
          "min": -0.0487
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 29409,
        "area_px": 740278,
        "density": 0.03973,
        "chars": 538,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 18.29
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        248,
        2411,
        2078,
        2698
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The Transportation Administration has been designated as the City Agency through which shall be routed for coordination all New York City Transit Authority dealings with the various City Administrations, departments, agencies and bureaus having jurisdiction over City-owned facilities other than Transit and affected by the design and construction projects.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2643,
          "min": -1.1655
        },
        "category": {
          "n_tokens": 1,
          "mean": -0.0,
          "min": -0.0
        },
        "text": {
          "n_tokens": 55,
          "mean": -0.0005,
          "min": -0.0221
        }
      },
      "ink": {
        "ink_px": 20251,
        "area_px": 509999,
        "density": 0.03971,
        "chars": 357,
        "chars_per_1k_ink": 17.63
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        248,
        2730,
        1973,
        2980
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The purpose of this directive is to provide all City Administrations, departments, agencies and bureaus and the New York City Transit Authority with one central office through which matters of mutual concern relating to the subway projects may be coordinated.",
      "logprob_stats": {
        "bbox": {
          "n_tokens": 21,
          "mean": -0.2267,
          "min": -1.4813
        },
        "category": {
